{"data":[{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110812068441915393"]},"author_id":"1687442525143912449","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:16:29.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110812070581018792"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":236,"start":218,"tag":"harvarduniversity"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/WTBbWSmKD5","end":260,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2110812070581018792/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110812068441915393","start":237,"url":"https://t.co/WTBbWSmKD5"}]},"id":"2110812070581018792","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":18,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Researchers led by Hengyun Zhou at MIT and collaborators have designed quantum error correction codes encoding more than one logical qubit for every two physical data qubits, a remarkably efficient use of redundancy.\n\n#harvarduniversity https://t.co/WTBbWSmKD5","url":"https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2110812070581018792"},{"author_id":"37804706","created_at":"2026-10-15T14:31:01.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110740231041265964"],"id":"2110740231041265964","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":9,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"A quantum computer isn’t a faster regular computer, it’s a different machine that only wins on certain problems, and it just got much more real.\n\nA regular bit is a 0 or a 1, while a qubit can sit in a blend of both and be linked to other qubits, which lets a quantum algorithm","url":"https://x.com/BXT66NYC/status/2110740231041265964"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110686879557271552"]},"author_id":"824786975580254209","created_at":"2026-10-15T10:59:02.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110686882153542010"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/BwsQGNIvzZ","end":301,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/QuantumAcad/status/2110686882153542010/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110686879557271552","start":278,"url":"https://t.co/BwsQGNIvzZ"}]},"id":"2110686882153542010","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":12,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"In December 2025, researchers at the University of Science and Technology of China reported that Zuchongzhi 3.2, a 107-qubit processor, had crossed the error correction threshold at code distance 7. Google's Willow team had published the same class of result 12 months earlier. https://t.co/BwsQGNIvzZ","url":"https://x.com/QuantumAcad/status/2110686882153542010"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110648575419969536"]},"author_id":"2057928733290565633","created_at":"2026-10-15T08:27:37.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110648778369663198"],"entities":{"cashtags":[{"end":135,"start":131,"tag":"QNT"},{"end":162,"start":157,"tag":"IONQ"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/XyEp0Q0qwz","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/QInvestorNotes/status/2110648778369663198/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110648575419969536","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/XyEp0Q0qwz"}]},"id":"2110648778369663198","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":409,"like_count":1,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Two logical gates can have similar average error rates and still behave differently in a long computation. For investors following $QNT and trapped-ion peer $IONQ, that matters when judging fault-tolerant roadmaps.\n\nA new Sandia-Quantinuum preprint applies gate set tomography to https://t.co/XyEp0Q0qwz","url":"https://x.com/QInvestorNotes/status/2110648778369663198"},{"author_id":"815942827968495616","created_at":"2026-10-15T19:27:24.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110814818697724401"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/BullTheoryio/s…","end":295,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/BullTheoryio/status/2110804484280713447","start":272,"url":"https://t.co/baf2qsMCZk"}]},"id":"2110814818697724401","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":25,"impression_count":9121,"like_count":123,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":21,"retweet_count":19},"text":"Is Bitcoin in trouble after Google's latest quantum computing breakthrough?\n\nShort answer: not today. But the gap is getting smaller.\n\nGoogle's new result makes one of the hardest parts of a quantum computer cheaper to build. That part is called \"magic states.\"\n\nBreaking https://t.co/baf2qsMCZk","url":"https://x.com/BullTheoryio/status/2110814818697724401"},{"author_id":"1757224886454439936","created_at":"2026-10-14T17:06:40.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110417013709660485"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/fhenix/status/…","end":301,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/fhenix/status/2110402267040121302","start":278,"url":"https://t.co/AfGs0liRys"}]},"id":"2110417013709660485","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":3,"impression_count":89,"like_count":13,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":5,"retweet_count":3},"text":"This is the most important framing of the quantum discussion I have seen recently. Most commentary focuses on hardware progress and qubit counts while missing the strategic logic that history already taught us. Your Enigma analogy is precise. Breaking a cipher is only valuable https://t.co/AfGs0liRys","url":"https://x.com/omer7890malik/status/2110417013709660485"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110613575643373568"]},"author_id":"73960501","created_at":"2026-10-15T06:08:39.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110613806757917109"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/lNZfaCAweD","end":243,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Rudolfdeleeuw/status/2110613806757917109/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110613575643373568","start":220,"url":"https://t.co/lNZfaCAweD"}]},"id":"2110613806757917109","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":18,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"𝗤𝗨𝗔𝗡𝗧𝗨𝗠 𝗩𝗦 𝗔𝗜: 𝗧𝗛𝗘 𝗡𝗘𝗫𝗧 𝗖𝗢𝗠𝗣𝗨𝗧𝗜𝗡𝗚 𝗥𝗘𝗩𝗢𝗟𝗨𝗧𝗜𝗢𝗡 𝗜𝗦 𝗔𝗟𝗥𝗘𝗔𝗗𝗬 𝗜𝗡𝗩𝗘𝗦𝗧𝗔𝗕𝗟𝗘 ⚛️🤖🚀\n\nAI is changing how we search, code, design and automate.\n\nQuantum computing could change something even deeper: the type of problems computers can https://t.co/lNZfaCAweD","url":"https://x.com/Rudolfdeleeuw/status/2110613806757917109"},{"author_id":"2070038718849929216","created_at":"2026-10-14T13:00:01.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110354943593066512"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":263,"start":246,"tag":"QuantumComputing"}]},"id":"2110354943593066512","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":0,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Physical qubits are fragile. The fix: a logical qubit.\n\nQuantum information is protected across correlations between physical qubits.\n\nCan't copy it (no-cloning theorem). Can't check it directly (would destroy it). Fix: check \"error syndromes.\"\n\n#QuantumComputing","url":"https://x.com/quantumsystmhub/status/2110354943593066512"},{"author_id":"2019406546761883648","created_at":"2026-10-15T16:47:08.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110774486031040999"],"id":"2110774486031040999","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":8,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Qubit errors fixed by DNA codes.\nOld: \"Surface code. 1000 qubits per 1 logical.\"\nNew: Encode logical qubit in DNA base-4\nMolecular QCA detects flip → CA triggers repair enzyme\nHopfield recall restores state\nBenefit: 1:20 overhead instead of 1:1000.\nThe qubit is protected by","url":"https://x.com/BenjaminIk67601/status/2110774486031040999"},{"author_id":"1868799136407097344","created_at":"2026-10-13T23:26:13.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110150144368775573"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":134,"id":"1881421472981303296","start":122,"username":"quipnetwork"}]},"id":"2110150144368775573","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":32,"like_count":1,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"One small disturbance can affect a qubit and compromise an entire quantum calculation. That’s why reliability matters for @quipnetwork.\nQuantum error correction uses multiple physical qubits to help detect and correct certain errors, protecting quantum information during","url":"https://x.com/TheKingpin05/status/2110150144368775573"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110666248623448064","3_2110666248715735041"]},"author_id":"849661480869912576","created_at":"2026-10-15T09:37:32.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110666375538827599"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/HE0UGV28XR","end":300,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/OptionKing666/status/2110666375538827599/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110666248623448064","start":277,"url":"https://t.co/HE0UGV28XR"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/HE0UGV28XR","end":300,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/OptionKing666/status/2110666375538827599/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110666248715735041","start":277,"url":"https://t.co/HE0UGV28XR"}]},"id":"2110666375538827599","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":489,"like_count":4,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":1},"text":"Quantinuum demonstrates the highest technical readiness among quantum pure plays, yet the market prices in the group's lowest commercial visibility, according to Morgan Stanley. On its 98-qubit Helios processor, protected operations proved roughly 4.3 times more reliable than https://t.co/HE0UGV28XR","url":"https://x.com/OptionKing666/status/2110666375538827599"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110823051646451712"]},"author_id":"2395227907","created_at":"2026-10-15T20:00:07.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110823053865164980"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/urvYEXoNwo","end":275,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Rondiskin/status/2110823053865164980/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110823051646451712","start":252,"url":"https://t.co/urvYEXoNwo"}]},"id":"2110823053865164980","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":1,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Scaling quantum hardware isn't just about qubit counts—it's routing. Transitioning from simple local coupling to multi-plane, high-connectivity layouts adds massive chip complexity, but it makes scalable quantum error correction mathematically viable. https://t.co/urvYEXoNwo","url":"https://x.com/Rondiskin/status/2110823053865164980"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110330533917921281","3_2110330536589742080","3_2110330538531725312","3_2110330540708474880"]},"author_id":"1855361322524753920","created_at":"2026-10-14T11:23:04.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110330542851797264"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"The most cited quantum research papers of every week since 2023, searchable by topic, year and week. Each one opens on arXiv in one click.","display_url":"aihorizonnetwork.com/papers/quantum","end":229,"expanded_url":"https://aihorizonnetwork.com/papers/quantum","start":206,"status":200,"title":"Quantum Papers | AI Horizon Network","unwound_url":"https://www.aihorizonnetwork.com/papers/quantum","url":"https://t.co/GhkIes5ad1"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/5M4ypALTA4","end":253,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/RaheelMali23426/status/2110330542851797264/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110330533917921281","start":230,"url":"https://t.co/5M4ypALTA4"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/5M4ypALTA4","end":253,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/RaheelMali23426/status/2110330542851797264/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110330536589742080","start":230,"url":"https://t.co/5M4ypALTA4"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/5M4ypALTA4","end":253,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/RaheelMali23426/status/2110330542851797264/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110330538531725312","start":230,"url":"https://t.co/5M4ypALTA4"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/5M4ypALTA4","end":253,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/RaheelMali23426/status/2110330542851797264/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110330540708474880","start":230,"url":"https://t.co/5M4ypALTA4"}]},"id":"2110330542851797264","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":12,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Error correction across the whole of IBM's 156-qubit ib